  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper introduces Quantum Differential Machine Learning (QDML) using parametrized quantum circuits to learn derivative prices and sensitivities. Simulator experiments show a 2‑qubit model achieving ≈0.069% mean relative error for European option prices and ≈0.258% for deltas, a 4‑qubit circuit learning Bermudan swaption prices with improved vega accuracy when trained with derivative information, and a 6‑qubit circuit trained on 8192 Monte Carlo samples to approximate basket option prices and deltas. All results are obtained via noiseless simulation without runtime or scaling comparisons to classical methods.",
